ed an eyelash  but instead it was used to build fake  tension I see a lot of people praising  this as a great way to get other  characters involved like piccolo Gohan  and tension hun but frankly I don't care  the outcome of a bad surprises if it's a  bad surprise that has an upside for  other characters that it shouldn't have  been a surprise in the first place it  should have just been delivered straight  there was no need for this to be a  mystery at all and only served to  disappoint a large portion of the  audience with all of that said however I  think this arc has more good than bad to  offer the series the only reason the bad  stands out so prominently in this arc  falls onto how these moments are written  into it the head writing contrivance  ease can slip through the cracks if they  are handled with subtle care but all the  major issues people have with this story  are such because the story so  prominently displays them for all to see  I love the concept of a character like  Mauro despite his somewhat bland  character motivation I love that  characters like vous and Vegeta are  featured so prominently in the story in  a very believable and natural way I'm  happy that namet made a comeback and  forced to yotaro to ease up on his use  of grey tones and even his paneling is  clear in places and not so much in many  others but I'll take what I can get I  want to dive deeper into this story  later on taking an in-depth look at  Marlowe's character specifically however  I'm gonna wait until the story is  complete before I do that the Galactic  Patrol saga is interesting it has its  ups and it's downs and despite having  quite a few troubled chapters I think  it's still a fun ride thanks for  watching  [Music]  you

